    "result_text": "All green. Build exits 0 and both acceptance tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to the owner create flow while keeping the flat `address` backward-compatible.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (`OwnerFields` schema) \u2014 added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` string properties, updated the `address` description to document that it's optional on input and always the composed/normalized value on output, and removed `address` from the `required` list so minimal and structured requests both validate. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` with the new getters/setters.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns with accessors so the structured fields round-trip through the database and are returned on GET.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the two new nullable columns to the `owners` table (hsqldb runs the tests with `ddl-auto=none`, so the explicit column is required there).\n\n4. **`src/main/java/.../owner/OwnerAddress.java`** \u2014 added `compose(addressLine1, addressLine2)`: the normalized line 1, with a single space and the normalized line 2 appended when line 2 is present. Normalization stays the single source of truth here.\n\n5. **`src/main/java/.../owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java`** \u2014 the create step now prefers the structured fields when `addressLine1` is non-blank (normalizing both lines, storing them, and setting the composed `address`), otherwise falls back to the normalized flat `address`. An owner is valid when it supplies an address in either form plus city; the composed `address` is what every later step (household hash, postcode/locality derivation) reads, since those operate on the stored value.\n\nMapStruct maps the new fields by name in both directions, so no mapper change was needed.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 exit 0; `AcceptanceTest` runs 2/2 green \u2014 `coreNormalizesAndComposesStructuredAddress` (structured `\"10 king st\"` \u2192 `addressLine1` and `address` both `\"10 KING STREET\"`) and `functionalityStillAcceptsFlatAddress`.",
